WHY AGPL-3.0
============

This project is not AGPL by preference; it is AGPL by obligation. The licence
of a combined work is decided by the strongest copyleft it links against, and
here that is Terracotta's AGPL-3.0.

    Component                     Licence        How it is used
    ----------------------------  -------------  -----------------------------
    Terracotta                    AGPL-3.0       bundled native library
                                                 (jniLibs/arm64-v8a/
                                                  libterracotta.so) + JNI
                                                 binding
    PojavLauncher core            GPL-3.0        JNI / EGL / OSMesa context
                                                 bridges, LWJGL and exec hooks,
                                                 Caciocavallo AWT stubs
    ZalithLauncher 2              GPL-3.0        launch-flow handling
                                                 (NeoForge classpath, Forge
                                                  processors, GLFW 3.4 stubs)
    EasyTier                      LGPL-3.0       inside Terracotta
    LWJGL (Pojav-patched)         BSD-3-Clause   lwjgl3/
    LWJGL 3.4.3 (self-built)      BSD-3-Clause   assets/lwjgl341/ (26.3)
    MobileGlues                   LGPL-2.1       libmobileglues.so,
                                                 libmobileglues_info_getter.so
                                                 (unmodified, dynamically loaded;
                                                  source: github.com/MobileGL-Dev)
    SDL3 (patched)                Zlib           libSDL3.so (26.3)
    shaderc / glslang / SPIRV     Apache-2.0     assets/lwjgl341/libshaderc.so
    OpenJDK (Temurin)             GPL-2.0 + CE   bundled JRE
    authlib-injector 1.2.8        AGPL-3.0       assets/authlib-injector.jar
                                                 (runtime Java agent; upstream
                                                  license notices are embedded)

GPL-3.0 code may be combined into an AGPL-3.0 work -- GPLv3 section 13 permits
exactly this -- and the result must be distributed under AGPL-3.0. That is what
this repository does.


CORRECTION TO EARLIER RELEASES
==============================

Earlier builds shipped an LGPL-3.0 LICENSE file, and the README described this
project's own code as "licence not declared". Both were wrong: the tree already
contained PojavLauncher core (GPL-3.0) and shipped libterracotta.so
(AGPL-3.0), so LGPL-3.0 was weaker than the combination allowed and leaving the
project's own code undeclared left the whole work ambiguous. The licence is now
AGPL-3.0, which is what the combination has required all along.


